  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_038: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) achieves 0.721 acc / 0.681 F1, clearly outperforming RNA-only multiprofile (0.653) and multimodal with resnet50 (0.688). However, the fusion strategy (concat vs. weighted) has never been tested in the multimodal setting—all completed multimodal runs used concat. Config_039 is identical to config_038 except for fusion=weighted, making it a clean single-variable test of whether learned/weighted fusion can further improve over simple concatenation in the strongest configuration. This is the best next experiment because: (1) it exploits the strong evidence that the scvi_n200 + ViT-L + transformer + multiprofile stack is the most promising direction, (2) it isolates the effect of fusion, an important and completely untested design axis, (3) it is a minimal one-variable change from the current best, avoiding confounds, and (4) under a limited budget, testing whether a small architectural tweak can push past 0.721 is more informative than exploring weaker encoder choices (e.g., scgpt, which scored 0.411 in single-profile RNA) or redundant aggregation comparisons (transformer vs. avgpool showed only a 0.003 gap in RNA-only)."
}

